-- title:
--   Special fibre of Drinfeld's formal upper half plane is a scheme
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and write $k_0 := W(k)/(p)$ for the quotient of the Witt vectors $W(k)$ by the ideal generated by $p$. The assertion is the existence of a scheme $Y$, a morphism $\pi_Y : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} k_0$ which is locally of finite type and separated, with $Y$ reduced, together with a family of bijections $e_Y$ indexed by the data of a Noetherian commutative ring $B$ carrying a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structure, a ring homomorphism $\psi : W(k) \to B$, a witness that $p$ is nilpotent in $B$, and the hypothesis $(p : B) = 0$; the bijection is between the set of morphisms $x : \operatorname{Spec} B \to Y$ such that $x$ followed by $\pi_Y$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map $W(k) \to k_0$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\psi)$, and the type $\mathrm{OmegaObj}$ of Deligne data over $B$ for $\mathbb{Z}_p \subset \mathbb{Q}_p$ with parameter $p$, i.e. assignments $M \mapsto \mathrm{line}(M)$ of a $B$-submodule of $B \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} M$ to each full $\mathbb{Z}_p$-lattice $M$ in $\mathbb{Q}_p^2$ with invertible quotient, compatible with lattice inclusions and with homotheties by $\mathbb{Q}_p^\times$, and satisfying the stated nondegeneracy condition at every prime ideal of $B$. Moreover these bijections are natural: for two such pairs $(B,\psi)$, $(B',\psi')$ and a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra homomorphism $g : B \to B'$ with $g \circ \psi = \psi'$, and any $y$ in the first set, $e_Y$ applied to $y \circ \operatorname{Spec}(g)$ equals $\mathrm{DeligneDatum.map}$ along $g$ of $e_Y(y)$ (the datum obtained by base change of each line along $g$).
--
--   This is the representability statement for the special fibre of Drinfeld's formal upper half plane after extension of coefficients to $W(k)/p$: the functor of Deligne data on Noetherian test algebras of characteristic $p$ is the functor of points, relative to $\operatorname{Spec} W(k)/p$, of a separated reduced scheme locally of finite type. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where it feeds the injectivity and bijectivity statements for the period map on special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in characteristic $p$.
